helping our wounded warriors find their  inner strength through a crossfit gym  yeah branded one crossfit is the first  and really only non-profit gym in las  vegas offering free memberships to  veterans while they work out with the  community victoria saha takes us through  their mission when we come across a  veteran we often say thank you for your  service but at branded one crossfit  veterans are being offered more than  just a thanks they're offered a free gym  membership the welcoming and the  atmosphere in here is what  made me want to come back here edward  haynes was in the marine corps for 20  years finding his way back to civilian  life wasn't the easiest keeping kind of  a community  has been  beneficial in keeping some of my sanity  you know finding michael like-minded  individuals in a place other than a than  a like a bar crossfit is a form of  high-intensity training haynes says it  reminds him of the brotherhood he felt  trying to accomplish a goal with other  marines when serving knowing that we're  going to share  some of the struggle again  you know  because struggle brings about a lot of  camaraderie are these your favorite  exercises  goodness  all right let's go haynes lets me join  in on a session along with equipment the  gym has soldier boots right at the  entrance and an american flag proudly  hanging adding to the welcome for those  who served what we want to do is get  them out of the house get them doing  something that's productive getting out  of their heads releases a lot of stress  and it helps you feel better  and that carries on for several hours  after you're done studies show since  2001 114 thousand vets have died by  suicide a scary statistic but branded  one is hoping to give our service men  and women another mission in life  besides carrying the weight of the  country it's not just about them though  right it's about bringing just regular  community members into the gym so that  hopefully they can just feel like  they're a 